{"name":"Lemon Lime Mojito","hex":"#cbba61","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lemon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A yellowish citrus fruit.","A semitropical evergreen tree, Citrus limon, that bears such fruits."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the flavour/flavor and/or scent of lemons.","Of the pale yellow colour/color of lemons."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lemon"},{"term":"lime","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any inorganic material containing calcium, usually calcium oxide (quicklime) or calcium hydroxide (slaked lime).","Any gluey or adhesive substance that traps or captures; sometimes a synonym for birdlime."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To treat with calcium hydroxide or calcium oxide (lime).","To smear with birdlime.\n To ensnare, catch, entrap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lime"},{"term":"mojito","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Cuban cocktail, generally made from rum, lime, sugar, mint, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mojito"}],"entries":[{"title":"List of lemon-lime drink brands","blocks":[{"text":"A lemon-lime soft drink or lemon-lime soda is a carbonated soft drink with lemon and lime flavoring."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Cider_%28lemon-lime_drink%29.jpg/330px-Cider_%28lemon-lime_drink%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_lemon-lime_drink_brands","wikidata":"Q1130245"},{"title":"Lemon","blocks":[{"text":"The lemon is a species of small evergreen tree in the Citrus genus of the flowering plant family Rutaceae. A true lemon is a hybrid of the citron and the bitter orange. Its origins are uncertain, but some evidence suggests lemons originated during the 1st millennium BC in what is now northeastern India. Some other citrus fruits are called lemon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/P1030323.JPG/330px-P1030323.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon","wikidata":"Q500"},{"title":"Mojito","blocks":[{"text":"Mojito is a traditional Cuban punch. The cocktail often consists of five ingredients: white rum, sugar, lime juice, soda water, and mint. Its combination of sweetness, citrus, and herbaceous mint flavors is intended to complement the rum, and has made the mojito a popular summer drink."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/15-09-26-RalfR-WLC-0072.jpg/330px-15-09-26-RalfR-WLC-0072.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mojito","wikidata":"Q487338"},{"title":"Lemon (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lemon or lemon-color is a vivid yellow color characteristic of the lemon fruit. Shades of \"lemon\" may vary significantly from the fruit's actual color, including fluorescent tones and creamy hues reflective of lemon pies and confections."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg/330px-Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon_(color)","wikidata":"Q2720565"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e3/Sprite_%28drink%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e3/Sprite_%28drink%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Sprite","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASprite_(drink).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/7_Up_-_You_like_it%2C_it_likes_you%2C_1948.jpg/500px-7_Up_-_You_like_it%2C_it_likes_you%2C_1948.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parse